---
import ProductLayout from '@/layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import { DUVET_SPECS } from '@/data/specs';
import { pageTitle } from '@/lib/seo';
---

<ProductLayout
  title={pageTitle('Hotel Duvet Covers')}
  description="Hotel duvet covers in percale, sateen stripe, mercerized cotton and jacquard, 180 to 250 cm wide. Wholesale."
  h1="Hotel duvet covers"
  breadcrumb="Duvet Covers"
  specs={DUVET_SPECS}
  images={['products-duvet-covers-hero']}
>
  <p>
    Duvet covers run 180 to 250 cm wide at 245 cm long and are cut to whatever insert the
    property uses. The cover size follows the duvet, not the bed, so send the insert dimensions
    rather than the mattress width.
  </p>
  <p>
    Four faces: percale for the standard programme, sateen stripe where the bed is part of the
    brand standard, mercerized for a brighter white, and jacquard where the pattern has to
    survive laundering rather than sit on the surface.
  </p>
  <p>
    Closure matters in a hotel more than it does at home. Buttons survive industrial pressing
    better than a flap, and a flap that does not sit flat looks untidy by the second wash. Tell
    us which the property's housekeeping expects.
  </p>
  <p>
    Construction, thread counts and cut-to-order minimums are on the
    <a class="font-semibold underline" href="/hotel-bedding-supplier/">hotel bedding supplier</a>
    page. The wider sheet range is on
    <a class="font-semibold underline" href="/hotel-linens/">hotel linens</a>.
  </p>
</ProductLayout>
